<% content_for :title, "Privacy · tinyslug" %>
<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
  <h1 class="font-mono text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">Privacy by design</h1>
  <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-ink-muted">tinyslug never stores a visitor's raw IP address. When link tracking is enabled, it records a daily rotating digest and coarse request metadata needed for aggregate reports.</p>
  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-lg font-semibold text-ink">What link owners can see</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-ink-muted">Reports can include visit counts, daily unique visits, country codes when a trusted local source is configured, referrer hosts, browsers, and device categories. Full referrer URLs and raw user agents are not retained.</p>
  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Your signals are respected</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-7 text-ink-muted">Tracking is skipped for Do Not Track, Global Privacy Control, recognized bots, and every link whose owner has disabled tracking.</p>
</article>
